# Furtive Courier's "This creature can't be blocked as long as you've sacrificed an artifact this turn" is about the Courier alone (CR 611.3a): after
# Bot1 sacrifices a Black Lotus, the Courier and Memnite attack together; Bot2's Grizzly Bears may not block the Courier but may block Memnite, which dies.
# The Courier's 3 damage gets through (the loot draws the Mountain and discards it, as the hand is empty).

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Memnite
Furtive Courier
Black Lotus
Island
Forest
Mountain
Island x11

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Jet
Mox Emerald
Grizzly Bears
Island x17

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Furtive Courier.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Grizzly Bears.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Attack(Furtive Courier > Bot2; Memnite > Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.DeclareBlockers]
! Bot2.Block(Grizzly Bears > Furtive Courier)
Bot2.Block(Grizzly Bears > Memnite)
[T3 Bot1.End]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 17
Bot1.Hand =
Bot1.Graveyard = Memnite; Mountain; Black Lotus
